description:
Follow-up to JMAP-tjvm.32 (closed): explore option (c) — typed constant-style property-name selectors for body_properties / properties parameters across all 7 sibling extension-client crates.

Current state: properties: Option<&[&str]> on every *_get method, body_properties: Option<Vec<String>> on EmailGetParams/EmailParseParams. Callers can typo property names with no compile-time signal; behavior depends on server leniency.

Proposed shape (per JMAP-tjvm.32 bead body):

  pub struct EmailProperty(pub Cow<'static, str>);
  impl EmailProperty {
      pub const ID: Self = Self(Cow::Borrowed("id"));
      pub const BLOB_ID: Self = Self(Cow::Borrowed("blobId"));
      // ... per RFC 8621 §4.1 ...
  }

Open design questions:

1. RFC 8621 §4.1.2 'header:*' selector pattern needs a constructor (e.g. EmailProperty::header("X-Custom-Field")) — raises complexity beyond plain constants.

2. Vendor extensions: workspace AGENTS.md policy excludes the Unknown(String) pattern for property-selector enums, but option (c)'s tuple constructor admits them. Is that acceptable?

3. Sweep scope: at minimum Email, EmailBodyPart, Mailbox, Thread, Identity, EmailSubmission for mail-client. Then propagation to the 7 sibling crates' equivalent types — likely 20+ typed property structs total, each with 5-25 constants.

4. Migration story: do existing &[&str] APIs deprecate alongside introducing &[EmailProperty]? Or break?

5. Breaking-change scope: this is a 0.2.0 or 1.0 candidate. Affects every /get method in the workspace.

Recommendation per the closed bead: defer to a 0.2.0 or 1.0-prep design pass. For 0.1.x the current Vec<String>/&[&str] surface is acceptable. Filing this bead to keep the design discussion tracked without blocking 0.1.x churn.
